# libretranslate
msgid "The SSO back-channel pin, added automatically. On an onion deployment the OIDC endpoints handed to an application are public ``.onion`` authorities. That is right for the browser, which reaches them through Tor, but unroutable for the application's own server-side calls (code-to-token exchange, JWKS, userinfo): a container resolves ``.onion`` through Tor's resolver, not through DNS. Pinning the provider to a reachable address sends those calls over the local network to the proxy that already serves the vhost. Skipped unless the application has SSO enabled and the provider vhost is an ``.onion`` name, so it is a no-op on clearnet."
msgstr "El perno del canal trasero SSO, añadido automáticamente. En un despliegue de cebolla los puntos finales OIDC entregados a una aplicación son públicos ``.onion`` autoridades. Eso es correcto para el navegador, que los alcanza a través de Tor, pero inestable para las llamadas del servidor de la aplicación (código a ficha, JWKS, userinfo): un contenedor resuelve ``.onion`` a través del resolución de Tor, no a través del DNS. Pinning the provider to a reachable address sends those calls over the local network to the proxy that already serve the vhost. Saltar a menos que la aplicación tenga habilitado SSO y el proveedor vhost es un ``.onion`` nombre, así que es un no-op en Clearnet."

