# libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Cuando la outa2-proxy SSO sabor es activo, el nativo de Snipe-IT ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` está habilitado a través de ``Setting`` modelo (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). puertas nginx ``/login`` a través de Oauth2-proxy/Keycloak e inyecta los verificados ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` encabezado, que Snipe-IT coincide con ``users.username`` (el usuario debe pre-existir y ser activado - sincronizarlos a través de LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitantes sin un usuario activado que coincida silenciosamente caen a través del formulario de inicio de sesión normal (no error). El formulario de inicio de sesión contraseña/LDAP se mantiene disponible como un inconveniente (``login_common_disabled = 0``), y el logotipo de la aplicación se redirige a la URL central de la sesión final de OIDC."

