msgid "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` La persona y las afirmaciones de la capacidad de referencia corren incondicionalmente."

msgid "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, so deploying this role is what switches the gateway from a weighted score to a System One decision."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` unconditionally."
msgstr "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` incondicionalmente."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` y corre en cada variante."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`) conduce el mismo viaje de administración y salta en la misma bandera."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` y afirma el proveedor, la URL base y el modelo, por lo que una superficie no configurada no puede alcanzar un despliegue verde."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, contraseña inutilizable) más su propio espacio de trabajo, y une el punto final a ese par."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` La persona y las afirmaciones de referencia funcionan incondicionalmente."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` y corre en cada variante."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` en cada variante de matriz, porque el ayudante del personaje compartido no puede conducir el registro de este papel en ninguno de ellos. Tres razones independientes, cada una suficiente por su cuenta:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: contrato de origen inmutable de un adaptador de repositorio. ``category_allowlist`` se adapta a una corriente superior que cambia las categorías enteras y no ofrece ningún filtro per-herramienta, donde una herramienta permitido sería inaplicable; ``mcp_passthrough`` delante de un río arriba que ya habla MCP en lugar de traducir REST. ``upstream_path`` nombres que arriba donde vive en el propio vhost de la aplicación, por lo que el proxy puede ocultarlo: alcanzarlo directamente pasa por encima de la lista de permisos que el adaptador existe para hacer cumplir. Un proveedor cuya corriente es un sidecar separado declara ``upstream_network`` y no tiene nada que ocultar allí."

# libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: lista de alias DNS. Default: ``[entity_name]`` para shared_net, ``[]`` para default_net"

# libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (por defecto ``True``): el archivo (o la entrada del título) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` prohibir el archivo/entrada sobre los papeles de este tipo para que la capa de forro pueda superar el delito con una razón precisa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` sólo lleva ``docker0`` una vez que el daemon ha corrido, y el config de daemon está escrito antes de que en un nodo fresco - los hechos se reúnen al principio del juego, y nada los re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-re-gathers después de la instalación. La lectura del hecho por lo tanto no produce nada en la misma carrera que tiene que emitir la dirección, que deja los contenedores interiores apuntan al solucionador de la red clara y el cheque DNS DinD fallando en un dominio sólo el nodo dnsmasq sabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (por defecto)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (por defecto) envolturas `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD funciona ~70 sub-roles para entregar Synapse, Element, cada puente soportado, Element Call y Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, y deshabilitar el paquete de MDAD Traefik / Postgres / Redis así que el Infinito central devuelve la pila."

# libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` es el público S3 endpoint y es accesible sin SSO gating."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` se lee de las variables de juego a menos que se ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` nombre el bloque en lugar de ``ports``, Para Discourse's archivo de lanzamiento, cuyo ``expose:`` lista es lo que se convierte ``docker run -p`` Ahí."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` del cliente haciendo el descubrimiento."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant tiene el token de la cuenta que la mintió. Este despliegue lo miente para el administrador, así que una llamada llega como el administrador que pidió al cliente. La exposición de la Entidad aún limita el alcance. Llegar al servidor de herramientas está cerrado en el papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost ata una llamada por la cuenta a la que pertenece la ficha. Este despliegue miente que el acceso personal a la cuenta de administrador, por lo que las llamadas llegan con los derechos de esa cuenta quien pidió. Alcanzar el servidor de herramientas está cerrado en el papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API token se emite contra la cuenta de administrador, por lo que cada llamada lleva los derechos de esa cuenta sin importar quién pidió al cliente. Alcanzar el servidor de herramientas está cerrado en el papel ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from managing Jenkins."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: la ficha de acceso personal se acuesta contra ``root`` y almacenados bajo ``administrator`` clave, así que cada llamada lleva los derechos de esa cuenta sin importar quién preguntó al cliente. Alcanzar el servidor de herramientas está cerrado en el papel ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from managing GitLab."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: la ficha de servicio web se emite contra la cuenta de administrador, por lo que una llamada lleva los derechos de esa cuenta independientemente de quién pidió al cliente. Las funciones adjuntas son sólo lectura, lo que limita lo que esos derechos pueden hacer aquí. Alcanzar el servidor de herramientas está cerrado en el papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Una llamada llega Baserow como el dueño de endpoint independientemente de quién le preguntó al cliente, y sólo alcanza el espacio de trabajo que cuenta posee. Ese es el segundo atado bajo el permisor del adaptador, no un sustituto."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud cuenta."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: identidad MCP llama ejecutada como. ``user`` y ``oidc`` adicionalmente requiere un ``delegation`` bloque, porque un portador de despliegue es una cuenta de servicio sin importar lo que digan los metadatos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` con el token de los datos del descubrimiento"

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: esquema de autenticación vigilando el punto final."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` es asesor y nunca falla la unidad - cada negativa se registra en la revista como ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, así que compruebe si un anfitrión espera que la instantánea no. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` falla la unidad, que es el punto de indicarla. Antes de cada instantánea el lanzador también elimina el ``.baudolo-*`` sobras de hojas muertas dentro de la raíz de datos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` o ``chezmoi``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (cuerda): directorio base para archivos CA"

# libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-limpia el esquema en una sesión psql y vuelve a reproducir el vertedero en el siguiente, por lo que un consumidor que bota entre recrea el esquema y la repetición muere por su cuenta ``CREATE TABLE``. Por lo tanto, la negativa mientras un consumidor se levanta."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` utiliza la central MariaDB’ ``root`` crear el DB por sitio en el primer despliegue."

# libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` sólo existe dentro EspoCRM a través de OIDC autoprovisionamiento (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas corren en cada variante."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` declara cuán firmemente un papel parejas al servicio que declara: ``>= 1`` mantiene al socio en el mismo anfitrión, ``< 1`` deja que viva sola. El valor se encuentra en el lado del consumidor de la relación, por lo que el par está dirigido y las dos direcciones de un par no necesitan estar de acuerdo."

# libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **padre** ``wiki.example.com`` (más ``example.com`` apex)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` ¿Dónde está? sys-ca-selfsigned la raíz CA en el anfitrión. Los objetivos de bind-mount del lado del contenedor viven en el ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) y llegar a los scripts de tiempo de ejecución independientes como env vars y argumentos CLI."

# libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: La contraseña de raíz para MariaDB servidor."

# libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (cuerda): ruta de acogida del certificado Root CA"

# libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: lo que este papel es en la auditoría MCP. Requerido."

# libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` es el mapa de comentarios per-key analizado desde default.env (ver :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Las claves dinámicas llevan sus comentarios a través de cada manejador ``COMMENT`` constante. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (ver :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` vuelve a reducir la salida estática cuando el contenido clonado cambia, por lo que los despliegues son impulsados por contenido sin ningún paso de compilación de tiempo de ejecución."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (deprecated)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` es el in-repo Docker Compose pila. Sigue siendo instalado pero no recibe nuevas características."

# libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` o ``swarm`` para clavar cada imagen a esa pista, ``rotate`` para dividir las imágenes en ambos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` falló."

# libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, sólo administrador en lugar de público"

# libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` es una decisión y simplemente reduce el resultado. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` y ``tools_unenforceable`` significa que el proveedor autorizó a este consumidor y la conexión todavía no puede ser renderizada, por lo que abortan la carrera en lugar de desaparecer tranquilamente: un cliente que silenciosamente termina con menos herramientas que el despliegue declarado es indistinguible de uno que funciona."

# libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: Anulación opcional"

# libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` para eliminar los recursos de Docker no utilizados."

# libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` para cada idioma, pero el lenguaje fuente, ``docs`` para los idiomas LibreTranslate soportes."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` es el único rechazo autorizado que no aborta, porque un proveedor que implementa más adelante en la misma obra no ha escrito su secreto todavía. Esa exención termina en la etapa de reconciliación, que funciona una vez que cada proveedor tiene: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` lo trata tan fatal allí."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: que principal el proveedor autentifica como, y donde se lee su secreto. Reemplaza el camino de señalización del administrador."

# libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, enviado como ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` es el archivo de anulación sin rastrear del operador; sus valores ganan sobre los valores estáticos por defectos Y los valores de control."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: El nombre de la base de datos inicial para crear."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: La contraseña para el usuario de la base de datos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: El nombre de usuario de la base de datos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (int): validez de certificado"

# libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` es donde docker toma esa dirección, así que la declaración responde antes de que el daemon exista y responde idénticamente después. Eso también lo mantiene daemon.json byte-identical cross passs, que el valor derivado de hecho no podía: apareció sólo de la segunda carrera en y reiniciaron el tiempo de ejecución del contenedor bajo una pila en vivo."

# libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: prueba grabada, en una versión previa exacta, que por usuario token adquisición, refresco, audiencia vinculante y revocación existen."

# libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` restringe a las funciones presentes en cualquier lugar ``groups``, que es lo que un consumidor de red de contenedores puede alcanzar realmente; ``all`` devuelve cada función declaratoria, desplegada o no."

# libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: ruta de destino (necesarios para ``cloud``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: si el papel expone el MCP, lo consume, o ambos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: El WP-ConsejoDiscourse pos de ida y vuelta. Disabling Discourse se salta; la capacidad de acceso de primera página y las bases de referencia CSP permanecen activas."

# libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` explícita ``name:`` sobre el terreno (alias for ``name``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: dominios canónicos y alias"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``)¡Corre! ``doli pull`` después de añadir asignaciones"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): paso ``--replace`` a ``doli add``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (necesarios): usuario para ejecutar ``doli`` como"

msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (bool)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: metadatos de conexión para clientes (funciones servidor solamente)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` cebollas cada fila capaz, ``disabled`` ninguno. ``exclusive`` deja caer las filas que no pueden tomar una, ``auto`` gira."

# libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` devuelve esas cadenas como una lista en lugar del bloque renderizado, para un contenedor que no se describe por un archivo de compostura en absoluto: ``web-app-discourse`` es construido por discourse_docker's ``launcher``, cuya única superficie de argumento es ``docker_args:`` en su ``app.yml``, así que necesita ``--add-host=<entry>`` líneas."

# libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` es una lista de hechos de la hoja de cálculo sobre el contenido del archivo. Cada entrada lleva la misma ``mandatory`` y ``allowed`` semántica descrita anteriormente y añade un ``marker`` bandera (por defecto ``False``): ``marker: True`` declara el camino como el marcador tipo para la entrada del tipo circundante. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` camina cada uno ``marker: True`` entrada; cada marcador que se resuelve a un valor no vacío en el archivo del papel añade el tipo circundante al conjunto tipo del papel. ``application_id`` para ``application`` y ``system_service_id`` para ``system-service`` son los marcadores canónicos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declara ``run-name:`` que interpola las entradas de envío. Una vez que una carrera ha comenzado, ese título es el único registro de ellos: el REST API respuestas ``inputs: null`` para un workflow_dispatch Corre. Cualquier cosa que quiera saber lo que una carrera fue despachada con por lo tanto se analiza el título, y parándolo contra un formato copiado a mano se derivaría en el momento en que el flujo de trabajo cambia, silenciosamente y sin una prueba de fracaso."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` publica el puerto de contenedores en un puerto de anfitriones, para un servicio dirigido sólo a través de la red de compostura."

# libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` es un opt-in explícito por servicio (falso) que hace que el servicio sea accesible sobre la cebolla del nodo: su puerto consigue un ``HiddenServicePort``. Porque ``applications`` es el config de la variante (base ``meta/services.yml`` profundamente fusionado con la ronda ``meta/variants.yml`` Anulación), un servicio se envía sólo en la variante/config donde se establece ``exposed: true`` — que es exactamente lo que permite que las dos variantes DB sean probadas sobre Tor (v0 expuesta - título accesible, v1 no se negó)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: que puede llegar al punto final."

# libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, cualquiera que sea el sitio de llamadas necesita en la parte superior: el VIP superpuesto de un par, o un servicio de pareja accesible sólo en el anfitrión."

# libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` mientras que los servidores MCP son descubiertos"

# libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` es ``os_family`` informes ansibles para el anfitrión. Llamadores que tienen hechos (el plugin de acción) pasarlo, así que las distribuciones fuera de la matriz CI - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - todavía resuelven a través de su familia. Llamadores sin hechos (lints, la prueba de disponibilidad) omitirlo y la familia se deriva de :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, que sólo cubre la matriz predeterminada."

# libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` sirve el archivo web UI detrás de un solo oauth admin2-proxy."

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (ejecutada en el host de despliegue) completa el mago de primera carrera (semillas de la administración de cristal), instala ambos plugins a través de Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` instalador, escribe el plugin configs, y reinicia."

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: configuración Playwright compartida"

# libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` lo valida al inicio. Un contrato que falta un límite, portando un permitido vacío, nombrando un camino comodín o careciendo de un schema pinchado hah se rechaza antes de que el proceso sirva a cualquier cosa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: lista de banderas a Y. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` elige la forma de la sonda (ver utils/docker/healthcheck/); cada sabor trae su propio intervalo, tiempo de salida, retries y start_period, y cualquiera de ellos puede ser superado junto a él. Sin un ``flavor`` la entrada debe llevar un explícito ``test`` Argv. ``port_key`` selecciona otra entrada abajo ``ports.internal`` para servicios que exponen su sonda en un segundo puerto."

# libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (bool): si es verdad, eliminar y regenerar la clave / cert"

# libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` es la lista de roles de proveedor que ``A`` depende directamente de (servicios que incrusta). ``reverse[B]`` es la lista de roles que dependen directamente de ``B`` (consumidores que incrustan ``B``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` honores nswitch y no puede dirigirse a un servidor, así que por su cuenta no puede decir cuál de los soluciones en resolv.conf rechazado. Donde la distro envía una herramienta de consulta, pregunte a cada servidor de nombres directamente; donde no lo hace, los veredictos por nombre todavía permanecen por su cuenta."

# libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` es la única fuente de verdad para los caminos de acogida. La capa env (utils/env/handlers, exportado por scripts/meta/env/load.sh) deriva el ``INFINITO_*`` claves env de ella; un env set gana para que los calladores puedan anular. Cuando una herramienta corre fuera de esa capa, por ejemplo, un desnudo ``subprocess`` que no hereda la construcción env, el valor se lee directamente del group_vars SPOT, por lo que todavía no hay defecto literal codificado duro."

# libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, que pins ``host.docker.internal`` en lo que llegue al host en el modo efectivo. Un contenedor que debe hablar con un servicio que el anfitrión publica - msmtp retransmitiendo a través de la ingress en enjambre en:587, por ejemplo - necesita el alias, y no debe código duro ``host-gateway`` porque eso se rompe bajo enjambre por la razón de abajo."

# libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, la propia red sólo"

# libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` sobre la superposición compartida del MCP"

# libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: cómo se proporciona la superficie, ordenada por precedencia."

# libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` existe porque una plantilla sirve a dos consumidores. El host /root/.msmtprc es leído por el host y el loopback es adecuado para él; la copia montada en /etc/msmtprc se lee dentro de un contenedor, donde 127.0.0.1 es el propio bucle de contenedor y nada escucha en él. Ese servicio también debe emitirse ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` Así que el alias resuelve."

# libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` colapsa todo al borde izquierdo - útil cuando la búsqueda se convierte en YAML de alto nivel (sin envoltura de servicio)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (por defecto) emite el corto ``\"host:published:container\"`` cuerda; ``host`` emite el bloque largo con ``mode: host``, que es lo que un papel de vanguardia necesita en en enjambre para que la dirección del cliente sobreviva al hop."

# libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (por defecto) lecturas ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reutiliza el puerto publicado, para servicios que no pueden remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, red de contenedores solamente"

# libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Kubernetes agente servidor, espacios de trabajo), ``pages``, ``registry`` y ``mailroom`` no están desplegados; ``gitlab.yml`` deshabilitarlos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (int): tamaño clave RSA"

# libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (cuerda): camino anfitrión a la llave privada Root CA"

# libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` nombres de la llave fija y predeterminados a ``version``; una entidad con varios pines declara una lista de tales bloques. Los tipos son ``git_tags`` (repositorio), ``registry_tags`` (imagen), ``npm`` (paquete), ``http_regex`` (url, patrón) y ``script`` (ruta, correr con la versión actual e imprimir la última)."

# libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: servicios.<key>.* base de búsqueda. Default: proporciona o entity_name"

# libretranslate
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` semillas el cursor de paginación OCI: sólo etiquetas clasificando lexically después de ser devuelto. Repos like GitLab GNC lleva decenas de miles de etiquetas de commit-sha antes de los ``v*`` etiquetas de liberación, así que un escaneo sin semillas se agota ``max_pages`` sin alcanzarlos nunca."

# libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` es el último compromiso de la rama predeterminada. Se construye al principio y se reconstruye cada vez que un fetch encuentra un nuevo compromiso; la construcción anterior se mantiene en línea hasta que el nuevo lo reemplaza."

msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: los tres escenarios RBAC dependen además de la sincronización del grupo LDAP; disabling LDAP los salta junto a OIDC."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` es el único camino que materializa un ``friendica.user`` fila, por lo que su habilitación se deriva directamente de la ``ldap`` bandera de servicio. El oauth2-proxy ``sso`` puerta en frente del vhost es una puerta de entrada de puerta delantera, no un puente de addon, y permanece en ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>` . La ruta de inicio de sesión LDAP está cubierta por la espectro existente LDAP Playwright (requisito 018), por lo que no se añade ninguna especificaciones específicas de addon."

# libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (Biblioteca de desencriptación AACS)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (Biblioteca de soporte de reproducción de Blu-ray)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` - marcador de madurez filtrado por ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: la solicitud, respuesta, tiempo fuera, concurrencia, paginación y techos de corriente la superficie impone."

# libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` sólo re-runs cuando la plantilla cambia"

# libretranslate
