# libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` y ``nocheck`` son aceptados como sinónimos (caso insensible) por este analizador. Por convención de repo cada regla de proyecto ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` DEBE utilizar ``nocheck:`` porque ``# noqa: <code>`` también es analizado por ruff como un flake8 directiva y disparadores ``invalid-noqa-code`` advertencias sobre cada clave de reglas específicas del proyecto. ``noqa:`` está reservado para el flake real8 / códigos ruff (``E402``, ``F401``, ...)El ``direct-yaml`` lint hace cumplir la convención al rechazar duramente la ``noqa:`` forma."

# libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` movimientos que comienzan deliberadamente: es cómo un operador alcanza la cola sin esperar nada. Por defecto 0, así que cada carrera que no pide que despliegue la misma cabeza y se puede comparar con la última. Esto solía derivarse del número de barrido en lugar, que compró cobertura de cola al precio de la cabeza - pedazo 0 Comenzó donde el aritmético apuntaba, las filas que más importaban corrían sólo cada pocos barridos, y no había dos carreras comparables."

# libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` y ``ldap-authenticator`` son mutuamente excluyentes auth backends (sólo uno puede ser habilitado; vea ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` Sólo lleva la coordenadas del instalador."

